        "created_at": "2025-07-25T07:05:08.101817+00:00",
        "notes": "In this round, picking your power is very important! Remember you are being an aggressive HEALER with this build!!\n\nIn my opinion, you have 4 options for this build:\nSelf-care: If you find yourself struggling to stay alive, but also wanting more item slots available for cooldown reduction, ability power, etc., this could work for you. Just keep in mind that it says \"3% of your max life,\" so if you don't have much health,h it will not be healing you for much.\nSupported shooting: If you are surviving just fine, but the team fights are lasting longer than they should be, or maybe your team is struggling a bit, this is another option to consider. \nTwo-zu: **Disclaimer: This could be good for you as an aggressive healer; however, if you pick this item, I would highly recommend using your 7th round power as a Cleansing charge. This will allow you to benefit from the two-zu; however, if you're going up against a DVA, for example, who absorbs projectiles, I would hesitate to pick this power. \n\nThe one power I would not recommend you pick would be: \n\nFleet foot: The reason I say do not pick this one is because you have spent this entire time building into cool down reductions, and the second line of this power says \" Cooldown is increased by 35% when used without a target.\" So if you have 35% cool-down reduction, then you just wasted all that stadium cash for no reason. I would save this build for an aggressive backline weapon power Kiriko, not an aggressive haler Kiriko.\n\nWith the way the abilities are now set up, you have more survivability while also maintaining your healing! The focus is still cool-down reduction, so you can bounce around and annoy the enemy team by being unkillable while also enabling your teammates to finish the enemy. Farm some cash while you're at it, too!",
